#: afc2452ecf0942f2ac91312227c10b16
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A directory user authenticates to a Sofia profile. After digest auth, "
"that user’s `user_context` selects the dialplan context. Vanilla internal"
" profile `context` is `public` (`conf/vanilla/sip_profiles/internal.xml`)"
" and applies to **unauthenticated** inbound only; users 1000–1019 have "
"`user_context=default` (`conf/vanilla/directory/default/1000.xml`). "
"Operator detail: [Chapter 6](https://developer.signalwire.com/freeswitch"
"/users-and-endpoints/user-directory), [Chapter "
"7](https://developer.signalwire.com/freeswitch/users-and-endpoints/sip-"
"profiles), [Chapter "
"12](https://developer.signalwire.com/freeswitch/dialplan/xml)."
msgstr ""
"号码簿用户向 Sofia profile 认证。认证后，该用户的 `user_context` 选择拨号计划上下文。Vanilla "
"internal profile 的 `context` 是 "
"`public`（`conf/vanilla/sip_profiles/internal.xml`），用于**未认证**入局；已认证用户 "
"1000–1019 的 "
"`user_context=default`（`conf/vanilla/directory/default/1000.xml`）。"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/0.getting-started/01-overview.md:133
#: c942a33730a04dd5bde730f1cc4a577f
msgid "Anatomy of a vanilla 1000→1001 call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/0.getting-started/01-overview.md:135
#: a6fdf540eeaf409e8568763add8a71fb
msgid ""
"**REGISTER.** 1000 registers to the internal profile "
"(`conf/vanilla/sip_profiles/internal.xml`). With `auth-calls` enabled, "
"Sofia challenges and checks `conf/vanilla/directory/default/1000.xml`. On"
" success it stores the Contact binding and loads user variables, "
"including `user_context=default` and caller-ID fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/0.getting-started/01-overview.md:136
#: ce79257922f24fd6bd3b7985286caa6d
msgid ""
"**INVITE.** 1000 sends INVITE for `1001`. After the same digest check, "
"routing uses `user_context` (`default`), not the profile’s "
"`context=public`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/0.getting-started/01-overview.md:137
#: cfc9be591a424a968a567198e19f736d
msgid ""
"**Dialplan match.** `mod_dialplan_xml` evaluates "
"`conf/vanilla/dialplan/default.xml`. `Local_Extension` matches "
"`^(10[01][0-9])$`; `$1` becomes `dialed_extension`. The extension sets "
"`call_timeout`, `hangup_after_bridge`, and `continue_on_fail` before "
"bridging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/0.getting-started/01-overview.md:138
#: 716f370ada6444dfbff4650461c56046
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Bridge.** `bridge` `user/${dialed_extension}@${domain_name}` looks up "
"1001 in the directory, takes the registered Contact, and originates the "
"B-leg. If the bridge fails and `continue_on_fail` is true, the same "
"extension continues into the voicemail fallback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/0.getting-started/01-overview.md:139
#: b627802a928e468f82364b08a33c96c4
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Media.** Internal `inbound-late-negotiation=true` defers A-leg codec "
"choice until B-leg SDP exists. Codec prefs come from "
"`$${global_codec_prefs}`. After 200 OK the channels are bridged and RTP "
"flows (pass-through when both legs share a codec)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/0.getting-started/01-overview.md:141
#: 35f20737aba3400eb3cd9fd39fad4a7d
msgid ""
"Track that call in the log by **session UUID**, not SIP `Call-ID` "
"([FAQ](../7.appendix/02-faq.md), "
"[Observability](../5.operations/02-observability.md))."
msgstr ""

